semantics(c3d1b36a) {
  name: "harness"
  scope: routed
  paths: [".agents/harness/", ".agents/records/", ".agents/ATLAS.md", ".claude/", "AGENTS.md"]
  cues: ["harness", "closure", "records", "template", "hook", "guard", "draft", "escalation", "atlas", "semantics card", "sync-settings"]
  holds: """
    harness/ holds templates, rules, hooks and tools, changed in substance only by the user; records/ holds state written only through bin/write.
    A template is both the form an agent follows and the schema the checker enforces; its first line names the store path under records/.
    The writer fills ids, numbers and file names; a draft that fails its template writes nothing.
    .claude/settings.json and bin/ are generated by sync-settings from hooks.json; sync-settings --check reports drift.
    Indexes, views, templates and the id ledger are refused to direct edits by guard-edit.
    Hooks stay thin: read the input, call a tool, return its exit code.
    """
  terms: """
    closure: a record written as nested (), [] and {}
    draft, stored, view: the three forms of one record
    escalation: a draft an agent could not fix, routed by a code in reasons.closure
    """
  next: """
    .agents/harness/README.md: the machinery
    .agents/harness/rules/RECORDS.md: kinds, commands and ids
    .agents/harness/rules/PRACTICES.md: restructuring docs, tools, hooks or records
    """
}
